IMPORT prelude

-- Judges' Remuneration Act 1994 (Singapore) -- who holds a "judicial office" and which retirement scheme an annual pensionable
-- salary counts for (s 1A), the salary and the floor under a Judge's allowances, and when pay starts, accrues and is paid (s 2), the
-- saving for Judges appointed before 1 September 1994 (s 3), and the gratuity on retirement or death for Judges first appointed on or
-- after 1 January 2015: who may get it, reckonable service, the amount as rate times complete months up to a limit, who receives a
-- death gratuity, and the bar on assigning or attaching it (s 4).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/JRA1994.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amending Act annotated in the text and listed in the Legislative History is Act 39 of 2019 (Judges' Remuneration (Amendment) Act
-- 2019, in force 2 January 2021). The source metadata records the version as current at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0180 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is five sections long, so the scope is all of it. The persons it applies to are the Judges themselves, their
-- dependants and estates, and their creditors (s 4(4)).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); s 2(1) and (4) beyond the rule that the salary is whatever the Minister's Gazette order says (no
-- order was retrieved, so no figure appears); s 4(3) (the President's power to make regulations) and s 4(6) (the Consolidated Fund
-- charge). The gratuity rate, its limit, the death gratuity and any "prescribed" circumstances and service are in regulations, which
-- were not retrieved: here they are inputs. What s 2(2)(b) of the repealed 1985 Act said (s 3) is not in the deposit.
--
-- Dates are written as numbers YYYYMMDD (e.g. 20150101).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example rows (the writing-l4-rules skill was not
-- available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Judges' Remuneration Act 1994`

§§ `1A -- judicial office and annual pensionable salary`

-- s 1A: "judicial office" means "the office of the Chief Justice, a Justice of the Court of Appeal, a Judge of the Appellate Division
-- or a Judge of the High Court". A Judicial Commissioner, a Senior Judge and an International Judge are not named.
DECLARE Office IS ONE OF
    `Chief Justice`
    `Justice of the Court of Appeal`
    `Judge of the Appellate Division`
    `Judge of the High Court`
    `Judicial Commissioner`
    `Senior Judge`
    `International Judge`

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a judicial office` IF
    CONSIDER `the office`
    WHEN `Chief Justice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Justice of the Court of Appeal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Judge of the Appellate Division` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Judge of the High Court` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 1A: "annual pensionable salary" means emoluments that count "(a) for a pension in accordance with the Pensions Act 1956 if the
-- holder is appointed to any judicial office before 1 January 2015; or (b) for a gratuity in accordance with this Act if the holder is
-- first appointed to any judicial office on or after 1 January 2015". The input is the date of FIRST appointment to a judicial
-- office; earlier service as a Judicial Commissioner does not count as a judicial office here.
DECLARE Scheme IS ONE OF
    `a pension under the Pensions Act 1956`
    `a gratuity under this Act`

GIVEN `first appointed on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Scheme
`the scheme the salary counts for` MEANS
    IF `first appointed on` LESS THAN 20150101
    THEN `a pension under the Pensions Act 1956`
    ELSE `a gratuity under this Act`

§§ `2 -- salary, allowances and when they are paid`

-- s 2(1): there must be paid to the Chief Justice, every Justice of the Court of Appeal, every Judge of the Appellate Division and
-- every Judge of the High Court "such annual pensionable salaries as the Minister may, from time to time by order in the Gazette,
-- determine". (4): the order "must be presented to Parliament as soon as possible after publication in the Gazette".
GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) requires a salary fixed by Gazette order` IF `is a judicial office` `the office`

-- s 2(2): a Supreme Court Judge receives allowances and privileges as the Minister may determine, "which must not be less than such
-- pensionable and non-pensionable allowances and privileges as a public officer receiving the same pensionable salary would receive".
GIVEN `the Judge's allowance` IS A NUMBER, `a public officer's allowance at the same salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the allowance meets the floor` IF
    `the Judge's allowance` AT LEAST `a public officer's allowance at the same salary`

-- s 2(3): salary or allowance "(a) commences from the date of appointment, but subject to the fulfilment of any condition on which
-- the allowance is payable; (b) accrues from day to day; and (c) is payable monthly on the last day of each month or on such other day
-- in each month as the Minister for Finance may from time to time determine".
GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `appointed on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `salary accrues for the day` IF `the day` AT LEAST `appointed on`

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER, `appointed on` IS A NUMBER, `the allowance's condition is fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an allowance accrues for the day` IF
    `salary accrues for the day` `the day` `appointed on` AND `the allowance's condition is fulfilled`

§§ `3 -- saving`

-- s 3: "Section 2(2)(b) of the repealed Judges' Remuneration Act (Cap. 147, 1985 Revised Edition) continues to apply to a Judge of
-- the Supreme Court appointed before 1 September 1994." What that paragraph said is not in the deposit.
GIVEN `appointed on` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the repealed s 2(2)(b) still applies` IF `appointed on` LESS THAN 19940901

§§ `4(7) -- reckonable service`

-- s 4(7): "reckonable service" means "(a) service in one or more judicial offices; (b) service as a Judicial Commissioner if, and only
-- if, it immediately precedes appointment to a judicial office without any break; or (c) such other service in the Government (except
-- as a Senior Judge or an International Judge) that regulations under this section prescribe to be reckonable ..., if, and only if,
-- that other service immediately precedes appointment to a judicial office without any break".
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `service in a judicial office`
    `service as a Judicial Commissioner`
    `prescribed Government service`
    `unprescribed Government service`
    `service as a Senior Judge`
    `service as an International Judge`
    `private practice`

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service, `it immediately precedes appointment without a break` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is reckonable` IF
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `service in a judicial office` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `service as a Judicial Commissioner` THEN `it immediately precedes appointment without a break`
    WHEN `prescribed Government service` THEN `it immediately precedes appointment without a break`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4(1), (5), (8) -- the retirement gratuity`

-- s 4(1): an individual "(a) who holds a judicial office; and (b) who retires from that office on attaining 65 years of age or in such
-- other circumstances as may be prescribed, MAY, on retirement, be granted by the President, in respect of each complete month of the
-- individual's reckonable service which is unbroken, a gratuity determined in accordance with a rate prescribed in regulations subject
-- to such limit as may be prescribed". (8): "This section applies only to an individual who is first appointed to any judicial office
-- on or after 1 January 2015." (5): "no holder of a judicial office has an absolute right to compensation for past services or to any
-- gratuity under this section."
GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office, `first appointed on` IS A NUMBER, `retired on attaining 65` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `retired in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be granted a gratuity` IF
        `is a judicial office` `the office`
    AND `first appointed on` AT LEAST 20150101
    AND (`retired on attaining 65` OR `retired in prescribed circumstances`)

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has an absolute right to a gratuity` IF FALSE

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- The amount: the prescribed rate for "each complete month" of unbroken reckonable service, "subject to such limit as may be
-- prescribed". The rate and the limit are inputs (regulations not retrieved). The months are whole months.
GIVEN `complete months` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed monthly rate` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed limit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the gratuity` MEANS `the smaller of` (`complete months` TIMES `the prescribed monthly rate`) `the prescribed limit`

§§ `4(2), (8) -- the death gratuity`

-- s 4(2): "Where at any time after 1 January 2015, an individual dies while holding any judicial office, there may be paid to such of
-- the deceased's dependants as the President may think fit or, if there are no dependants, to the legal personal representatives of
-- the deceased, a death gratuity determined in accordance with regulations." (8) limits the section to those first appointed on or
-- after 1 January 2015.
DECLARE Payee IS ONE OF
    `the dependants the President thinks fit`
    `the legal personal representatives`
    `no one under s 4(2)`

GIVEN `the office` IS AN Office, `first appointed on` IS A NUMBER, `died on` IS A NUMBER, `has dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Payee
`who may be paid the death gratuity` MEANS
    IF (NOT `is a judicial office` `the office`) OR `first appointed on` LESS THAN 20150101 OR `died on` AT MOST 20150101
    THEN `no one under s 4(2)`
    ELSE IF `has dependants`
         THEN `the dependants the President thinks fit`
         ELSE `the legal personal representatives`

§§ `4(4) -- assignment and attachment`

-- s 4(4): a gratuity "(a) is not assignable or transferable, except for the purpose of satisfying -- (i) a debt due to the Government;
-- or (ii) an order of any court for the payment of periodical sums of money towards the maintenance of the spouse or former spouse or
-- minor child, whether legitimate or not, of the individual ...; and (b) is not liable to be attached, sequestered or levied upon for
-- or in respect of any debt or claim except a debt due to the Government."
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `a debt due to the Government`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a spouse`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a former spouse`
    `a periodical maintenance order for a minor child`
    `a periodical maintenance order for an illegitimate minor child`
    `a periodical maintenance order for an adult child`
    `a lump-sum maintenance order for a spouse`
    `a bank loan`
    `a private judgment debt`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gratuity may be assigned to satisfy it` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for a spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for a former spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for a minor child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a periodical maintenance order for an illegitimate minor child` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gratuity may be attached for it` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a debt due to the Government` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
